# =============================================================================
# Files NOT uploaded to Vercel.
#
# Vercel only builds the Next.js frontend (app/, components/, contexts/, lib/,
# public/ + the root config files). Everything else in this repo belongs to the
# API or the satellite pipeline and is either large, secret, or both.
#
# Size matters: ml-service/ alone is ~750 MB on a working checkout (venv,
# datasets, trained .joblib artifacts, user uploads). Shipping it would blow
# past the deployment upload limit and slow every build for zero benefit.
#
# Same exclude-list strategy as .dockerignore: anything not listed here IS
# uploaded, so a newly added frontend directory works without touching this file.
#
# NOTE: .vercelignore is applied when a deployment is created from the `vercel`
# CLI. Git-integration deployments clone the whole repository instead, so for
# those the build simply never reads these paths — the Next.js build only
# traces from app/ and its imports either way.
# =============================================================================

# --- Backend / ML, none of which the frontend build imports ------------------
ml-service
satellite-ml
# Hugging Face Space build context (Dockerfile + api entrypoint).
spaces

# --- Container + deployment tooling ------------------------------------------
Dockerfile.web
.dockerignore
docker-compose.yml
docker-compose.*.yml
deploy

# --- Docs ---------------------------------------------------------------------
docs
README.md
*.md

# --- Data files ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Datasets and model artifacts. Belt-and-braces: the directories above already
# cover the known ones, these catch stray copies at any depth.
*.csv
*.parquet
*.joblib
*.pkl
*.h5
*.onnx
*.tif
*.tiff
*.geojson
*.zip
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3

# --- Python -------------------------------------------------------------------
# No Python is part of the frontend build; this also covers scripts/*.py.
**/*.py
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/.venv
**/venv
**/.pytest_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/.mypy_cache

# --- Secrets ------------------------------------------------------------------
# Env values come from the Vercel dashboard, never from an uploaded file.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*-service-account*.json
*-sa-key*.json

# --- Local build state / editor / OS ------------------------------------------
.next
out
node_modules
**/node_modules
*.tsbuildinfo
.git
.claude
.vscode
.idea
**/.DS_Store
